From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: ltr501: wait for the start-up time after power-on

The probe enables the vdd and vddio supplies and reads the part ID
straight away. The LTR-559 needs 100 ms after power-on before it
answers on the bus, so on a board where the supplies are switched on by
this probe the read fails and the probe returns the I2C error without a
message.

On a Redmi 4 Prime (LTR-559 on an i2c-gpio bus, vdd from a PM8953 LDO)
the sensor was left unbound at every boot, while binding it by hand
after boot read part ID 0x92 and probed cleanly. Wait the start-up time
after enabling the supplies.

---
 drivers/iio/light/ltr501.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/iio/light/ltr501.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/light/ltr501.c
@@ -1449,6 +1449,12 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, ret,
 				     "Failed to get regulators\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * The chip ignores the bus until its start-up time after power-on
+	 * has passed (100 ms on the LTR-559).
+	 */
+	msleep(100);
+
 	data->reg_it = devm_regmap_field_alloc(&client->dev, regmap,
 					       reg_field_it);
 	if (IS_ERR(data->reg_it)) {
